{% doc %}
  Renders ONE child-bearing level-1 desktop menu item as a content-sized
  dropdown card, replacing Horizon's full-viewport mega-menu band for that
  item. Rendered from the §4(c) wrap at
  blocks/_header-menu.liquid#nav-dropdown; items WITHOUT children fall through
  to the untouched native `<li>` in that same wrap.

  Every class, ref and attribute core relies on is preserved deliberately:

  - `class="menu-list__list-item"` on the `<li>` — `overflow-list` counts and
    re-slots its children by that class, so the "More" flyout keeps working.
  - `on:focus="/activate"` / `on:blur="/deactivate"` and NO
    `on:pointerenter` / `on:pointerleave` (decision D5). Core JS is uneditable,
    so omitting the pointer attributes is the only lever that removes
    hover-to-open: assets/component.js dispatches purely off the attribute and
    refuses the `closest()` fallback for pointer enter/leave, so an absent
    attribute means the event can never reach this item. Keeping focus/blur
    preserves focus-open and blur-close — the latter is the established
    focus-out dismissal. (Horizon 4.1.4 removed `on:focus` from the NATIVE
    item, moving keyboard-open onto a dedicated disclosure button; this card
    keeps D5's focus-open deliberately — its trigger is already a real button,
    so Enter/Space toggle too — and the focus-driven `activate` is also what
    keeps core's own state writes, `inert` clearing and the transparent-header
    `header-menu[aria-expanded]` signal in the loop for every BMP open.)
  - `ref="menuitem"` on the trigger and `ref="submenu[]"` on the panel —
    assets/header-menu.js resolves both through those refs (`findMenuItem`,
    `findSubmenu`); since 4.1.4 `findSubmenu` reads
    `listItem.querySelector(':scope > [ref="submenu[]"]')`, so the panel must
    stay a DIRECT CHILD of this `<li>`.
  - `inert` on the panel, exactly like the 4.1.4 native submenu: it keeps the
    collapsed card out of the tab order and the accessibility tree, and the
    header's row-elevation rule (sections/header.liquid) keys on
    `.menu-list__submenu:not([inert])`, so a panel that never carried the
    attribute would keep the row permanently elevated. Core's activate /
    deactivate toggle it on the focus/blur paths and
    assets/bmp-header-menu.js mirrors it on the click / Escape /
    outside-press paths.
  - `data-skip-node-update="true"` on the trigger — it must survive the idle
    header hydration morph, exactly as the native `<a>` does.
  - `aria-expanded` on the trigger is the SINGLE state signal (R6). Core's
    `#expandableFor` (4.1.4) writes the state onto a `[ref="disclosure[]"]`
    button when one exists and falls back to the `[ref="menuitem"]` element
    when none does — this card ships no disclosure, so core keeps writing the
    trigger on focus/blur, assets/bmp-header-menu.js writes it on click /
    Escape / outside-click, and the CSS reveal needs no second mechanism.

  The trigger is a `<button>`, not an `<a href>` whose navigation is cancelled
  (decision D2) — that role conflict is v1.1.5 bug #7. The parent collection
  stays reachable as the panel's first row (D3), which is also where
  `aria-current="page"` belongs, since a button never navigates.

  `data-bmp-submenu-size` on the card carries the merchant's Submenu size
  option. The stock preset `submenu-font-styles` writes inverts
  levels 2 and 3 on Medium/Large — level 2 small and subdued, level 3 large and
  foreground — because it was written for Horizon's mega-menu, where level-2
  entries are column headers above a list of links. This card is a cascading
  list, so consuming those vars literally renders children bigger and darker
  than their parents. The card re-derives its own size/colour map from this
  attribute (assets/bmp-styles.css, the submenu size-map block in the nav
  dropdown group): every submenu row renders ONE size per option (14/16/18,
  product decision 2026-08-19), with hierarchy carried by colour and indent.
  Family, weight and case still come from the stock vars, which is why the
  `submenu-font-styles` render below stays.

  @param {object} link - The level-1 link. Must have `link.links` present; the
    caller gates on that.
  @param {number} index - `forloop.index` of the link in the caller's loop, used
    to build the `submenu-N` id the trigger's aria-controls points at.
  @param {object} block_settings - The header-menu block's settings, forwarded to
    `submenu-font-styles`.
  @param {string} [background_color_classes] - Scheme classes the caller already
    computed for the submenu (`color-custom-<block.id>`,
    `background-matches-parent`).

  @example
  {% render 'bmp-nav-dropdown',
    link: link,
    index: forloop.index,
    block_settings: block_settings,
    background_color_classes: background_color_classes %}
{% enddoc %}

<li
  class="menu-list__list-item bmp-nav-item"
  on:focus="/activate"
  on:blur="/deactivate"
>
  <button
    type="button"
    data-skip-node-update="true"
    class="menu-list__link button-unstyled bmp-nav-trigger{% if link.active %} menu-list__link--active{% endif %}"
    aria-controls="submenu-{{ index }}"
    aria-haspopup="true"
    aria-expanded="false"
    ref="menuitem"
  >
    <span class="menu-list__link-title">{{- link.title -}}</span>
    <span class="bmp-nav-trigger__caret">
      {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
    </span>
  </button>
  <div class="menu-list__submenu bmp-nav-panel{{ background_color_classes }}" ref="submenu[]" inert>
    <div
      id="submenu-{{ index }}"
      class="menu-list__submenu-inner"
      style="{% render 'submenu-font-styles', settings: block_settings %}"
    >
      <div
        class="bmp-nav-panel__card"
        data-bmp-submenu-size="{{ block_settings.menu_font_style | default: 'regular' }}"
      >
        {%- for group in link.links -%}
          {%- assign group_panel_id = 'bmp-nav-group-' | append: index | append: '-' | append: forloop.index -%}
          <div class="bmp-nav-group" data-bmp-nav-group>
            <div class="bmp-nav-group__title">
              <a
                href="{{ group.url }}"
                class="bmp-nav-group__link"
                {% if group.current %}
                  aria-current="page"
                {% endif %}
              >
                {{- group.title -}}
              </a>
              {%- if group.links != blank -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="button-unstyled bmp-nav-group__toggle"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-controls="{{ group_panel_id }}"
                  aria-label="{{ 'bmp.accessibility.bmp_nav_expand' | t: title: group.title }}"
                >
                  <span class="bmp-nav-group__caret">
                    {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                  </span>
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- if group.links != blank -%}
              <div id="{{ group_panel_id }}" class="bmp-nav-group__panel">
                {%- comment -%}
                  role="list" is not redundant: Safari/VoiceOver drops list
                  semantics from a <ul> whose list-style is none, which
                  .list-unstyled sets. Stock has the same gap in
                  snippets/mega-menu-list.liquid; this is the cheap half.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <ul class="bmp-nav-group__list list-unstyled" role="list">
                  {%- for item in group.links -%}
                    <li>
                      <a
                        href="{{ item.url }}"
                        class="bmp-nav-group__item"
                        {% if item.current %}
                          aria-current="page"
                        {% endif %}
                      >
                        {{- item.title -}}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</li>

